Here's a bug I think I have located in 3.1.1 (Mac). I don't know if anybody has
mentioned anything like this before, so here goes:

On one game I was playing recently, one of my characters died while in a shop.
When another character came in, he entered the shop and proceeded to pick up
some of the items left behind by the previous character. Some of the items gave
a message that went somewhat like:

 "Item not on payed list. perhaps you'd better quit."

Or something like that. My recollection of the exact message is a bit hazy. What
I _think_ happened was that the previous character (the one who created the
bones file) had been carrying some items which hadn't been payed for when he
died. Then havok broke loose when my new character tried to pick them up again.
But my recollection of this whole episode is a bit vague. Could someone comment
or try to confirm this?


